  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the GC8 Funding Request in Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Initiation Plan (PIP) comprises UNDP&#x2019;s support to the Government of Angola in developing a high quality Funding Request to the Global Fund for the upcoming funding cycle. The proposal will focus on scaling up priority interventions to prevent and treat HIV, including reducing mother to child transmission; prevent and control tuberculosis, including multidrug resistant TB; and reduce malaria morbidity and mortality nationwide, in line with national policies and Global Fund priorities.As UNDP has been selected as the Principal Recipient for Grant Cycle 8, this support will strengthen the technical quality and strategic alignment of the Funding Request while enhancing grant readiness. The PIP will contribute to effective programme design, coordination, and positioning UNDP to support timely and successful grant implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
